# Cloudflare Tunnel runtime config + credentials for the 24/7 telemetry
# bridge -- config.yml embeds a real tunnel ID and a path to the
# credentials JSON, which is a bearer secret for that tunnel. Only the
# .example template is tracked.
/cloudflared/config.yml
/cloudflared/*.json

# Scheduled-task wrapper log output for the 24/7 telemetry bridge.
/scripts/logs/

# Python artifacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# C++ / Visual Studio build outputs
x64/
Debug/
Release/
*.obj
*.exe
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.iobj
*.ipdb
*.lib
*.exp
*.tlog
*.recipe
*.lastbuildstate
.vs/
.vscode/

# OS files
.DS_Store

# Microsoft Office lock/temp files (created while a .docx/.xlsx/.pptx is open)
~$*

# Runtime generated benchmark / telemetry output
BENCHMARK_REPORT.json
benchmarks/SOAK_TEST_REPORT.json
telemetry_data.bin
telemetry_stream.bin

# benchmarks/generate_benchmark_report.py's compiled animus_benchmark_suite
# binary -- already covered by the blanket *.exe pattern above on Windows,
# but named explicitly since the directory also holds a Linux/macOS build
# with no extension, which *.exe would miss. benchmarks/BENCHMARK_REPORT.md
# (the generated report itself) is NOT ignored -- it's meant to be
# committed as a real, reproducible snapshot, same as BENCHMARKS.md.
benchmarks/_build/
AnimusCore_v1/secure_demo_tenant10.log
AnimusCore_v1/cluster_demo_node*.log

# Native library staged into animus/ by setup.py's build_py override
# (see Phase 6) -- built per-platform, never tracked in source control.
# Also covers bindings/animus_py.cpp's compiled nanobind extension
# (animus/_animus_native.*), whether staged there by the local
# direct-CMake dev loop (bindings/CMakeLists.txt's own instructions) or
# copied in some other way -- same "built per-platform, never tracked"
# rule applies.
animus/*.dll
animus/*.so
animus/*.dylib
animus/*.pyd

# Same rule for sdk/python/animus_sdk/'s compiled nanobind extension
# (csrc/animus_ring_buffer.cpp) -- see sdk/python/CMakeLists.txt's local
# dev-loop instructions for how it's staged there.
sdk/python/animus_sdk/*.dll
sdk/python/animus_sdk/*.so
sdk/python/animus_sdk/*.dylib
sdk/python/animus_sdk/*.pyd

# Any stray *.whl from a local `pip install ./bindings` or `./sdk/python`.
bindings/*.whl
sdk/python/*.whl

# Phase 8: demo mTLS certs + private keys generated by
# AnimusCore_v1/generate_demo_certs.ps1 for secure_transport_demo.cpp --
# never commit private key material, even a demo-only one.
AnimusCore_v1/demo_certs/

# Proprietary-edition licensing: the RSA private key that signs license
# files (license_tools/generate_license_keypair.ps1) must never be
# committed -- anyone with it can mint a license for any machine. The
# public key (animus_license_pubkey.hpp) is generated alongside it and
# IS meant to be committed; only this directory is excluded. NOT a
# blanket "*.lic" pattern -- license_tools/test_fixtures/*.lic are
# committed test fixtures (signed for a fingerprint that can never match
# a real machine, so publishing them reveals nothing usable), and a
# blanket pattern would silently exclude those too.
AnimusCore_v1/license_tools/private/
.vercel
.env*

# W-8BEN generator: never commit real PII (PAN, home address, DOB) or a
# filled tax form, to this repo or any repo -- this one has a public
# GitHub remote and deploys via Vercel. The config holds real personal
# data; the generated PDF embeds it. Both are local-only, gitignored
# regardless of where they're generated. See scripts/generate_w8ben.py.
scripts/.w8ben_config.json
docs/W8BEN_*_prefilled.pdf
.cache/
# Broadened 2026-09-03 pre-flight audit: a real, signed W8BEN was found
# sitting untracked at AnimusCore_v1/W8BEN_Alakshendra_Roy_(Official
# Document).pdf -- outside the docs/*_prefilled.pdf pattern above, so a
# careless `git add -A` would have staged it. Catch any W8BEN-named PDF
# anywhere in the tree, not just the generator's own output path.
**/W8BEN_*.pdf
**/*W8BEN*Official*.pdf

# Local benchmark-reproduction output (benchmarks/telemetry_benchmark.cpp
# writes this to the invocation directory per BENCHMARK_DATASHEET.md's own
# documented repro commands) -- not a deliverable, shouldn't get committed
# by anyone following those instructions.
/telemetry_benchmarks.json

# Pilot client license files (animus_pilot_*.lic) generated for evaluation
# -- tied to specific customer machine fingerprints, same "never commit"
# reasoning as AnimusCore_v1/license_tools/private/ above.
eval_keys/

# Regenerable via eval_kit/scripts/package_kit.sh -- a packaged snapshot,
# not a source artifact, so never worth tracking.
/animus-eval-kit-v*.tar.gz

# 2026-09-07 pre-flight audit: an unrelated third party's personal
# document, a payment screenshot, a business card, and a screen recording
# were all found sitting untracked in AnimusCore_v1/ -- none belong in a
# repo with a public GitHub remote. Kept on disk, never committed.
AnimusCore_v1/Harini_S_Ibbani_Template_TNR12_No_Languages.pdf
AnimusCore_v1/Payment.jpeg
AnimusCore_v1/Animus_Business_Card.pdf
AnimusCore_v1/Screen recording.mp4

# Logo/icon exploration duplicates superseded by the tracked
# animus-logo-mark.png -- never committed, so they don't compete with it.
AnimusCore_v1/Animus Logo.jpeg
AnimusCore_v1/animus-logo.png
AnimusCore_v1/logo.png
/animus-icon.png

# CMake+Ninja build directory for a Linux-target build (produced e.g. by
# running deploy_verify.sh under WSL) -- same "build output, never
# tracked" rule as build/ above, just a different directory name.
build_linux/

# Personal-use executive dashboard + its live telemetry bridge. Contains
# real outreach data (which firms, exact invite counts) and internal
# directives that must never land in this public repo's history. Was
# briefly committed at dd315a1 -- do not push that commit; kept local-only.
/command-center.html
/command_center_bridge.py
/.command_center_bridge_scratch.log

# Self-issued .lic for the command-center bridge above, signed for this
# specific dev machine's fingerprint (MachineGuid + MAC) so the dashboard's
# license-gated features (core pinning) work locally -- same "machine-
# specific, personal-use, never public repo" reasoning as eval_keys/ above.
/customer.lic

# Internal 5-year strategy/execution blueprint: real cash-on-hand and burn
# figures, deal-mix math behind the ARR targets, and an explicit "base
# case vs. stretch target" gap analysis -- same never-public-repo category
# as command-center.html above, for the same reason (real financial and
# competitive-strategy detail, not a client-facing document).
/docs/ROADMAP_2026_2031.md

# Outbound outreach working tracker: names, employers, and real LinkedIn
# profile URLs for 20+ real third-party individuals, plus candid sales-
# targeting commentary about them ("verify before using", pitch angles) --
# real personal data about people who never consented to being profiled in
# a public repo, same never-public-repo category as command-center.html
# above (that entry's own reasoning -- "real outreach data ... must never
# land in this public repo's history" -- was written for exactly this kind
# of file but never applied here until a 2026-09-09 audit caught it).
# Removed from tracking via `git rm --cached`; still on disk as a working
# local tracker. NOT scrubbed from prior commit history -- if that's ever
# needed, it's a deliberate, separate history-rewrite decision, not a
# side effect of this gitignore entry. docs/ICP_TARGET_LIST.md stays
# public -- company-level research only, no named individuals.
/docs/OUTBOUND_TRACKER.md

# Screen recording of the personal-use command-center dashboard -- same
# never-public-repo category as command-center.html itself above (shows
# the same real outreach data and internal directives on screen).
/AnimusCore_v1/dashboard.mp4

# NOTE: docs/dashboard.html used to be a local recreation of the outbound
